<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29047" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῠσ-ηχής</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῠσ-ᾱχής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠχέω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ill-sounding</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Po.</u>
				2.16
			</span></i>, v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Comp.</u>
				14
			</span></i>; <i>giving a dull sound</i>, of metals, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.721c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσθμοῖο δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					100.19
				</span></i>
			:— in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, epith. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλεμος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.686
			</span></i> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				Anacr.
				107
			</span></i>), al.; and of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάνατος</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				16.442
			</span></i>, al. (where it should perh. be taken, =
			<i>bringer of great woe</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄχος</span>),
			cf. <i><span class="en">
				Apollon.
				<u>Lex.</u>
			</span></i>), of 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φόνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					136.1
				</span></i>
			; <i>of ill-repute</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἀνδράσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Ap.</u>
					64
				</span></i>
			.</div>
